[
    {
        "content": "<p>I would like to ask, to avoid issues similar to <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/defeq.20abuse.20in.20.60WithLp.60/near/462136240\">#mathlib4 &gt; defeq abuse in &#96;WithLp&#96; @ 💬</a>   how one decides the right approach?</p>\n<p>For example, had the old definition of <code>WithLp</code> been unexposed, then the issue of original post would have never happened:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ENNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ENNReal</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If the examples are put into another file, they still give error and if I expose <code>WithLp</code>'s definition, then the examples do work as expected. Now, defining <code>WithLp </code> as a one field structure also solves the problem. By why is it a better solution? In general, how one decides the right approach?</p>",
        "id": 608512555,
        "sender_full_name": "Paradoxy",
        "timestamp": 1783362095
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I just want to say that when WithLp was changed to a structure the expose mechanism did not exist)</p>",
        "id": 608516404,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1783363582
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The disadvantage of the <code>no_expose</code> approach is that one loses the def-eq <code>WithLp.ofLp (WithLp.toLp x) = x</code>.</p>",
        "id": 608518079,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1783364241
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"648495\">Christian Merten</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unexposed.20definitions.20or.20one.20field.20structures.3F/near/608518079\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The disadvantage of the <code>no_expose</code> approach is that one loses the def-eq <code>WithLp.ofLp (WithLp.toLp x) = x</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>And why would one want this property in the first place?</p>",
        "id": 608827421,
        "sender_full_name": "Paradoxy",
        "timestamp": 1783454832
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Independently of the exposure, the one field structure is a good idea because it not only creates but  forces the use of casting functions</p>",
        "id": 608829462,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783455577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Those casting functions are essential as they provide keys for <code>simp</code>, and prevent ending up with goal states that are invisibly in the wrong type.</p>",
        "id": 608829826,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783455718
    }
]